<title>GREECE: NATL MORTGAGE SETS JUNE 30 BOND RATE AT 10.4PCT.</title>
<headline>NATL MORTGAGE SETS JUNE 30 BOND RATE AT 10.4PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's National Mortgage Bank set the gross rate on its bonds maturing June 30 1997 to 10.40 percent, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>National Mortgage bonds expiring on June 30 may be rolled over at a gross 10.40 percent rate provided they have been issued less than five years ago, it said.</p>
<p>Bond returns are subject to a 15 percent withholding tax, it said. --Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
